        "original_id": "092dbfb2-c4d8-5e02-b0ba-48497780afc2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: New York–New Jersey border, northeast coast of North America\n- Organizations: Province of New York, Province of New Jersey\n- Events: New York–New Jersey Line War\n- Topics: colonial boundary disputes, British colonies\n\nFacts:\n- The Province of New York existed from 1664 to 1776 as a British proprietary colony and later a royal colony on the northeast coast of North America.\n- The New York–New Jersey Line War, also called the N.J. Line War, was a series of skirmishes and raids that occurred between 1701 and 1765.\n- The New York–New Jersey Line War took place at the disputed border between the Province of New York and the Province of New Jersey.\n- The New York–New Jersey Line War lasted for more than half a century.",
